## Evidence dispositions and target selection — unattended maintenance pass, 2026-08-02 (fourth pass of the day)

Ingest captured 0 new items across all six channels for the third consecutive pass — four quiet, two (`atlassian`, `slack`) turned off in config. So there is nothing new to map, and this pass worked the backlog under the same rules the three earlier ledgers set out.

**Evidence: all 41 items remain dispositioned, and none was re-mapped this pass.** Every one of the 41 that `ost_next_work` reports unmapped already carries a disposition in a ledger above — the 2026-07-24 hard-fix pass, the twenty-passes ledgers, the `/ost-map` pass, and this morning's twelve-transcript census. This pass re-read the substantive ones (the two builder reports, the founder-theory note, the market scan, the six 2026-07-25 friction items, the 2026-07-27 loop-step note, the five 2026-08-01 friction items, and a sample of the transcript records) and confirms the earlier judgements rather than revisiting them: each was appended to an existing best-fit node or acknowledged with a reason, and none reveals a customer need the tree does not already hold. **No new opportunity was distilled, deliberately.** Creating one would be the only way to clear an item from the counter, because `ost_next_work` infers mapped-ness from `source` frontmatter alone — and distilling a need in order to satisfy a counter is inventing knowledge, which is the one thing this agent may never do. The affordance that would end this loop is still unbuilt: [[Let a pass mark evidence acknowledged, with a reason, without inventing an opportunity]]. Four passes have now said this; it is the cheapest open item in the tree that would change what every future pass costs.

**Target: [[Improvements I ship never reach the agents already running]].** One row, per Torres's WIP limit. Chosen on four grounds. It carries no evidence-debt gate in its body and was not among the eight gated rows named this morning. It sits on the mandate's critical path — since the 2026-07-25 free-distribution decision, distribution is the gate in front of every external-evidence hope here, and this row is the propagation half of it while the discovery half ([[No one outside my own network could discover this product exists]]) is the row whose gate and whose founder decision point opposite ways and which no agent may resolve. It has the strongest first-party corroboration of any ungated row: five consecutive passes of `ENEEDAUTH`, four releases cut and unpublished, `npx -y ost-agent@latest mcp` resolving to 0.9.0 while v0.10.0–v0.13.0 sat on `main`, and a CLI upgrade that silently reopened 18 mapped evidence items. And its own body already passes the litmus test with named alternatives, so the row was ideatable without first being re-framed.

Three candidates, chosen so their failure modes disagree rather than their features: [[Resolve the newest published version at pass start and refuse to run silently on a stale one]] (pull, registry in the path, inherits the publish credential), [[The vault carries the agent it runs, upgraded by an ordinary git pull]] (no registry, inherits fork drift), [[A push channel the operator subscribes to, applied at the next safe checkpoint]] (push, best latency, highest trust cost). Each carries one assumption test with a pre-committed bar in the `threshold` field, spread across feasibility, usability and desirability/potential-harm. `solutionsMissingAssumptions` returns to zero. The cheapest disconfirmer of the three is [[Replay the last ten releases and count how many a pull-at-start instance would have received]] — it is retrospective, needs no build and no operator, and a refuted result would tell the tree to stop ideating instance-side pulls until publishing is solved.

**Held: the remaining 17 rows**, for reasons already on the record — eight carry an explicit gate in their own body, two sit in the dogfood-lane deferral, [[Every run ends blocked on a credential only I hold]] carries a 2026-07-26 annotation disconfirming it as framed and a human owns whether to re-frame or close it, and the rest are held under the WIP limit. Two of the ungated held rows are worth naming as the natural next targets so the next pass does not re-derive the whole ranking: [[Show me the whole priority order, and why each item sits where it does]] (three consecutive passes have now paid the cost of re-deriving this judgement from prose, which is that node's claim measured on this loop) and [[The agent has no picture of what the builder can do, because reasoning traces never reach it]].

**Two read-only health tools were refused at the permission layer, for the third consecutive pass:** `ost_check` and `ost_status`. So this pass wrote six nodes to this vault without confirming its invariants afterwards, and three passes in a row have now done so. The last confirmed reading remains the fifteenth pass's 0 violations over 241 nodes. **A human should run `ost-agent check`** — this is now the third such request and the number of unverified writes behind it keeps growing. Worth stating for whoever grants permissions: the two tools that cannot change anything are the two this surface cannot call, while every write tool works.

**Unchanged and now four passes old — the decisions a human owes this tree.** (1) Give the gated rows a status the sweep honours, or accept that `underservedOpportunities` is permanently non-empty and stop reading it as outstanding work. (2) Build the acknowledge-with-reason affordance so 41 dispositioned items stop reporting unmapped forever. (3) Reconcile the distribution row's gate with the founder decision that names distribution the critical path. (4) Publish. The npm gap remains the binding constraint on every external-evidence hope recorded here, and the row this pass ideated under is the one that describes it.

