## 2026-08-03, unattended sweep — one new need, four rows ideated, twenty-eight held

**Ingest.** One new item across six channels: `USAGE:2026-08-02` (240 calls, 235 ok, 5 failed, 8 sessions). Atlassian and Slack remain disabled in config. Twenty-five items were outstanding; **all twenty-five were read in full**, not from excerpts.

**Mapping — one node created, six dispositioned onto existing nodes.** Twenty-two of the twenty-five items are session-friction records, and reading them together rather than one at a time is what made them worth anything: the same six patterns recur across the set, and five of the six already have a node.

- **New:** [[The file changed after I read it, and the failed edit is how I find out]] — six sessions, same refusal (`String to replace not found in file`) against text the agent had just read, and one session (`424486ec`) that recorded the cause in the same breath as the symptom: another process had moved HEAD and touched ~14 files seconds earlier. Distinct from [[Two agents sharing my vault can trample each other]] (damage to shared state) and from [[Two thirds of my calls failed, and each one only told me after I made it]] (learning what *exists* from a refusal). Sourced at `observed` — TRANSCRIPT provenance is a recording.
- **Corroborated, no node:** [[My loop spends its time waiting for a check it cannot subscribe to]] gained **twelve sessions across eleven distinct PRs** — it was created from one. [[The work I most want to run unattended is the work that keeps needing a decision]] gained sixteen stops across eight sessions, including `7e982096`, whose *only* friction was seven clarifying questions and zero tool errors. [[The same refusal is rediscovered every session, because nothing carries the lesson forward]] gained the strongest form of its own evidence: `(eval):1: == not found`, five times in a row inside one session. Also appended: [[The agent has to guess what resources it's actually working with]], [[The same agent has a different tool surface on every surface I run it on]], [[Two thirds of my calls failed, and each one only told me after I made it]].

**The 2026-08-02 trace deserves its own line.** 240 calls at a 2% failure rate, against the 67% day this tree already holds — strong confirmation that the bad day was a condition of that day, not a background rate. But **all five failures are the same failure**: `ost_create_node` refused three separate nodes for declaring `stated` against a `channel:inbox` source whose ceiling is `assertion`. One unlearned rule, paid for five times, inside this product rather than in the shell around it.

