None of those four carries an explicit gate — they are unlisted operational rows of the kind the 2026-08-02 third pass chose, and they block the discovery loop itself. **But four rows is not one row, and Torres's WIP limit is one.** The cause is the same one this ledger has now recorded twice: this pass ideated under three rows before reading the Prioritization section, which is authoritative and is not visible from `ost_next_work`. Ideating under the row it created from new evidence was within precedent; the other three were a judgement made without the governing document in hand. Recorded as a decision to review, not defended as a plan.

